		<div class="topic" id="forum_op_topic_572679490124250790">
		How can I travel to other map locations outside the world that has been generated?	</div>
	<div class="content" id="forum_op_content_572679490124250790">
		It keeps generating places like towns, houses, and cities. I don't want that. I want the ability to generate other types of locations after creating a city, such as forests, dungeons, or other areas. Having the entire story take place in the same location is starting to get boring.	</div>
		
	<div class="forum_op_footer">
		<div></div>
			</div>
</div>
<div data-featuretarget="community-awards"></div>
<script type="text/javascript">
	$J( function() {
		InitializeForumTopic( {"owner":"46277277","type":"General","feature":"0","gidforum":"590692129307765155","forum_display_name":"General Discussions","forum_url":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/app\/5103870\/discussions\/0\/","forum_search_url":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/app\/5103870\/discussions\/search\/","is_public":1,"permissions":{"can_view":1,"can_post":1,"can_reply":1,"is_banned":0,"can_delete":0,"can_edit":0},"appid":5103870}, "https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/forum\/46277277\/General\/",
		"572679490124250790", {"author":"Arilade","text":"\nIt keeps generating places like towns, houses, and cities. I don't want that. I want the ability to generate other types of locations after creating a city, such as forests, dungeons, or other areas. Having the entire story take place in the same location is starting to get boring."}		);
			} );
</script>
										<script type="text/javascript">
$J( function() { InitializeCommentThread( "ForumTopic", "ForumTopic_103582791475798685_590692129307765155_572679490124250790", {"feature":"590692129307765155","feature2":"572679490124250790","owner":"103582791475798685","commentthreadid":"662343330","total_count":6,"start":0,"pagesize":15,"has_upvoted":0,"upvotes":0,"votecountid":null,"voteupid":null,"commentcountid":null,"subscribed":false,"extended_data":"{\"topic_permissions\":{\"can_view\":1,\"can_post\":1,\"can_reply\":1,\"is_banned\":0,\"can_delete\":0,\"can_edit\":0},\"original_poster\":199507057,\"topic_gidanswer\":\"0\",\"forum_appid\":5103870,\"forum_public\":1,\"forum_type\":\"General\",\"forum_gidfeature\":\"0\"}","oldestfirst":true,"comments_raw":{"572679490124257750":{"text":"I don't think the other areas works yet, well I can't seem to get it to.","author":"PeaceMaker"},"572679490124303476":{"text":"Expanded map\/locations in general is prioritized highly; rough ETA about 1 month","author":"AI Roguelite: AI-generated RPG"},"572679490124316400":{"text":"[quote=AI Roguelite: AI-generated RPG;572679490124303476]Expanded map\/locations in general is prioritized highly; rough ETA about 1 month [\/quote]\n\nI will wait for that. At least now I got a new character that I created for me to play in the story.","author":"Leisha"},"572679490124326505":{"text":"[quote=Leisha;572679490124316400][quote=AI Roguelite: AI-generated RPG;572679490124303476]Expanded map\/locations in general is prioritized highly; rough ETA about 1 month [\/quote]\n\nI will wait for that. At least now I got a new character that I created for me to play in the story. [\/quote]\nYou should try putting in rules that make the AI absurdly funny. i was laughing my ass off at some of the conversations they have.","author":"LCD"},"572679770568945835":{"text":"[quote=Arilade]It keeps generating places like towns, houses, and cities. I don't want that. I want the ability to generate other types of locations after creating a city, such as forests, dungeons, or other areas. Having the entire story take place in the same location is starting to get boring. [\/quote]\n\nYou are running exactly into the \"overwriting\/painting\" bug and engine limitation I\u2019ve been analyzing! Right now, the game's engine heavily restricts the AI by forcing it into a traditional RPG framework. It completely lacks the developer tools to properly expand, rename, or cleanly shift already placed zones on the map, which causes it to just cram everything into the original floor space instead of creating large new zones. \n\n[b]I actually just started a megathread specifically to collect these kinds of engine limitations and bugs for Max Loh:[\/b]\n[url=https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/app\/5103870\/discussions\/0\/572679490124313468\/]Click here to join the Megathread[\/url]\n\nPlease feel free to post your findings over there as well! I'm trying to gather all reports in one structured place so the developer can see exactly what needs to be fixed for the upcoming update to truly unlock the game's sandbox potential.","author":"simon500732"},"572679770568946672":{"text":"[quote=AI Roguelite: AI-generated RPG;572679490124303476]Expanded map\/locations in general is prioritized highly; rough ETA about 1 month [\/quote]\n\nThank you so much for responding! Your presence here means a lot to the community.\n\n[b]To make things much easier for you, I have started a centralized Megathread here:[\/b]\n[url=https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/app\/5103870\/discussions\/0\/572679490124313468\/]Click here to view the Megathread[\/url]\n\nSince there are quite a few duplicate discussions popping up, I took the liberty of pointing players from connected threads over to this central post so they can share their bug reports, findings, and engine limitations there. I really hope having all this structured data in one single discussion helps you pinpoint what needs tweaking for the upcoming update!","author":"simon500732"}},"track_navigation":true}, 'https://steamcommunity.com/comment/ForumTopic/', 40 ); } );
</script>
