						16 hours ago&nbsp;
					</div>
				</div>

				
				<div class="commentthread_comment_actions" >
														<a class="forum_comment_action forum_comment_action_trigger" data-tooltip-type="selector" data-tooltip-content="#forum_comment_actions_menu_572679770568945835">
					<span><i class="ico16 arrow_down"></i></span>
				</a>
			
			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_572679770568945835">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791475798685', '590692129307765155', '572679490124250790', '81728080', '572679770568945835' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_572679770568945835">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b>Arilade</b>:</div>It keeps generating places like towns, houses, and cities. I don't want that. I want the ability to generate other types of locations after creating a city, such as forests, dungeons, or other areas. Having the entire story take place in the same location is starting to get boring. </blockquote><br>You are running exactly into the &quot;overwriting/painting&quot; bug and engine limitation I’ve been analyzing! Right now, the game's engine heavily restricts the AI by forcing it into a traditional RPG framework. It completely lacks the developer tools to properly expand, rename, or cleanly shift already placed zones on the map, which causes it to just cram everything into the original floor space instead of creating large new zones. <br><br><b>I actually just started a megathread specifically to collect these kinds of engine limitations and bugs for Max Loh:</b><br><a class="bb_link" href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/5103870/discussions/0/572679490124313468/" target="_blank" rel="" >Click here to join the Megathread</a><br><br>Please feel free to post your findings over there as well! I'm trying to gather all reports in one structured place so the developer can see exactly what needs to be fixed for the upcoming update to truly unlock the game's sandbox potential.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
									<div></div>
				
				
									<div class="forum_comment_permlink">
						<span class="forum_comment_moderate">
													</span>
												<a data-panel="{&quot;focusable&quot;:false}" href="#c572679770568945835">#5</a>
											</div>
							</div>
